# UniverseStudio License (USL) 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 the UniverseStudio authors.

This is a **source-available copyleft** license with a no-sale term. It is
deliberately **not** an OSI "open source" license, because it forbids selling. In
plain words: you may use UniverseStudio for anything — **including commercial work**,
such as a photographer or studio using it on paid jobs — and you may study, change
and fork it freely; every fork must stay open under these same terms; but nobody may
**sell** the software itself or lock any of it behind a price, a subscription or a
"premium" tier. The limit is on selling the software, not on what you make with it.

This license may be referred to as the **USL**, and this version as **USL 1.0**.

## 1. Definitions

- **"Software"** means UniverseStudio and the contents of this repository, **except**
  any component that carries its own separate license. Separately-licensed components
  are not covered by this license and keep their own terms — in particular the
  UniversePen SDK and its API documentation (MIT), and any third-party code noted in
  NOTICE.md. Where such a component is present, its own license governs it.
- **"You"** means anyone exercising the rights in this license.
- **"Fork"** / **"Derivative"** means any work based on or containing part of the
  Software, in any form (a changed copy, a port, a larger work that includes it).
- **"Sell"** means to charge money or other payment for the Software or a Derivative,
  or for access to it or any part of its functionality — including selling it,
  licensing it for a fee, bundling it in a paid product or paid service, putting it
  behind a paywall or a required purchase, charging a subscription or recurring fee,
  gating any feature behind a paid tier, "premium", "pro" or paid unlock, or selling
  in-app purchases, add-ons or upgrades for it. Accepting voluntary donations that
  are not a condition of access and unlock nothing is not selling.

## 2. What you may do

Subject to the conditions below, you are granted a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive license to:

- run and use the Software for **any purpose, including commercial work** (for example
  editing images for paying clients) — using it is never restricted;
- study and modify its source;
- fork it and make Derivatives;
- share the Software and your Derivatives with anyone, for free.

## 3. Conditions

1. **Stay open (copyleft).** If you distribute the Software or any Derivative — as
   source or as a built app, to anyone, including over a network — you must also
   make the **complete corresponding source** of what you distributed available to
   every recipient, at no charge, and license that whole work under **this same
   license**, version 1.0. You may not add terms that restrict the rights granted
   here, and you may not relicense it (no MIT, no proprietary, no sublicensing).

2. **No selling, no paid tiers.** You may not Sell the Software or any Derivative. In
   particular, a fork may not add premium features, paid tiers, subscriptions, in-app
   purchases, or any paid unlock: every feature of a distributed fork must be
   available to every user at no charge. You may not charge for it, for access to it,
   or for a product or service whose main value is it.

3. **Keep the notices.** Keep this license, the copyright notice, and the author
   credits intact in all copies and Derivatives. State prominently if you changed
   the files.

4. **No misrepresentation.** Do not claim the original authors endorse your Derivative,
   and do not use their names or marks to promote it without permission.

## 4. Termination

If you breach these conditions and do not cure the breach within 30 days of becoming
aware of it, your rights under this license end automatically for the versions you
hold. Rights of others who received copies from you in compliance are not affected.

## 5. No warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
